H5114.def:
A man of the Arabs living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 25:15; 
son of: Ishmael (H3458); 
brother of: Nebaioth (H5032), Kedar (H6938), Adbeel (H0110), Mibsam (H4017), Mishma (H4927), Dumah (H1746), Massa (H4854), Hadad (H2301), Tema (H8485), Jetur (H3195), Naphish (H5305) and Mahalath (H4258); also called Nodab at 1 Chroniques 5:19; 
Another name of qe.de.mah (קֵ֑דְמָה "Kedemah" H6929) 
§ Nodab = "nobility"
an Arab tribe probably descended from Nodab, son of Ishmael and grandson of Abraham

H5119.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Genèse 46:21; 
son of: Benjamin (H1144); 
brother of: Bela (H1106A), Becher (H1071), Ashbel (H0788), Gera (H1617), Ehi (H0278), Rosh (H7220), Muppim (H4649), Huppim (H2650H), Ard (H0714), Ahiram (H0297) and Jediael (H3043); also called Nohah at 1 Chroniques 8:2; 
Another name of na.a.man (נַעֲמָן "Naaman" H5283G) 
§ Nohah = "rest"
the 4th son of Benjamin

H5126.def:
A man of the tribe of Ephraim living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exode 33:11; 
son of: Elishama (H0476); 
father of: Joshua (H3091) 
§ Nun = "fish" or "posterity"
father of Joshua the successor of Moses

H5146.def:
A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Genèse 5:29; 
son of: Lamech (H3929H); 
father of: Shem (H8035), Ham (H2526) and Japheth (H3315)
Also named: Nōe (Νῶε "Noah" G3575) 
§ Noah = "rest"
son of Lamech, father of Shem, Ham, and Japheth; builder of the ark which saved his family from the destruction of the world which God sent on the world by the flood; became the new seminal head of mankind because his family were the only survivors of the flood

H5152H.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 11:26; 
son of: Terah (H8646); 
brother of: Abraham (H0085), Haran (H2039) and Sarah (H8283); married to Milcah (H4435) and Reumah (H7208); 
father of: Uz (H5780H), Buz (H0938), Kemuel (H7055), Chesed (H3777), Hazo (H2375), Pildash (H6394), Jidlaph (H3044), Bethuel (H1328A), Tebah (H2875), Gaham (H1514), Tahash (H8477) and Maacah (H4601)
§ Nahor = "snorting"
1) son of Serug, father of Terah, and grandfather of Abraham
2) son of Terah and brother of Abraham

H5176I.def:
A woman living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 2 Samuel 17:25; 
wife of: Jesse (H3448H); 
mother of: David (H1732), Eliab (H0446I), Abinadab (H0041I), Shimeah (H8093), Nethanel (H5417H), Raddai (H7288), Ozem (H0684), Zeruiah (H6870), Abigail (H0026H)(?) and Elihu (H0453J)
§ Nahash = "serpent"
1) a king of the Ammonites during the time of king Saul
2) the father of Abigail, the mother of Amasa, the commander of Absalom's army

H5177.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Exode 6:23; 
son of: Amminadab (H5992); 
brother of: Elisheba (H0472); 
father of: Salmon (H8007)
Also named: Naassōn (Ναασσών "Nahshon" G3476) 
§ Nahshon = "enchanter"
son of Amminadab and prince of the Judah at the first numbering in the wilderness; 5th in descent from Judah in the genealogy of Christ

H5179.def:
A woman living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2 Rois 24:8; 
daughter of: Elnathan (H0494); married to Jehoiakim (H3079); 
mother of: Jehoiachin (H3078) 
§ Nehushta = "brass"
daughter of Elnathan, wife of king Jehoiakim of Judah and mother of king Jehoiachin of Judah

H5184I.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Samuel 1:1; 
son of: Zuph (H6689); 
father of: Elihu (H0453); also called Nahath at 1 Chroniques 6:26; Toah at 1 Chroniques 6:34; 
Another name of to.chu (תֹּחוּ "Tohu" H8459)
§ Nahath = "rest"
1) one of the dukes of Edom, son of Reuel and grandson of Esau
2) a Kohathite Levite, son of Zophai and grandson of Elkanah
3) an Levite overseer in the time of Hezekiah
